# MongoDB connection string for leaderboard (used in all environments when set).
# Copy this file to .env.local and set your URI so dev, build, and custom server all use it.
# If the database is not updating, check:
# 1. .env.local exists and contains MONGODB_URI (no leading space, no quotes unless the value contains spaces).
# 2. Run with: npm run dev (Next.js loads .env.local) or npm run dev:server (custom server loads .env.local).
# 3. In the terminal, look for "[Leaderboard] MONGODB_URI is not set" — if you see it, the API is not using the DB.
#
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017
# Or Atlas: MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster.mongodb.net/
